WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.360
Cameras are common payloads for still imagery and video.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.389
Mission requirements determine resolution, field of view, stabilization, frame rate,

00:00:07.389 --> 00:00:08.419
and capture interval.

00:00:08.419 --> 00:00:12.033
Higher settings increase storage and processing without automatically improving the

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:12.558
decision.

00:00:12.558 --> 00:00:16.603
Thermal sensors measure emitted energy and can support inspection or search tasks at a

00:00:16.603 --> 00:00:17.313
high level,

00:00:17.313 --> 00:00:21.502
but interpretation depends on calibration, environment, surface properties, distance,

00:00:21.502 --> 00:00:22.737
and operator competence.

00:00:22.737 --> 00:00:26.457
A thermal image does not directly measure every condition a viewer may infer.

00:00:26.457 --> 00:00:30.716
Mapping payloads and software combine overlapping observations into products such as

00:00:30.716 --> 00:00:32.026
orthomosaics or models.

00:00:32.026 --> 00:00:36.625
Useful mapping requires appropriate overlap, consistent coverage, position quality,

00:00:36.625 --> 00:00:38.195
and documented processing.

00:00:38.195 --> 00:00:40.755
The final product should state accuracy and limitations.

00:00:40.755 --> 00:00:44.729
Metadata may include time, position, altitude estimate, device, camera settings,

00:00:44.729 --> 00:00:45.874
and software history.

00:00:45.874 --> 00:00:50.654
It supports organization and analysis but may also expose sensitive locations or

00:00:50.654 --> 00:00:51.059
operations.

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:53.753
Preserve needed metadata while controlling distribution.

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.513
Match the payload and collection pattern to the mission purpose.

00:00:56.513 --> 00:00:58.443
Collecting extra views, private areas,

00:00:58.443 --> 00:01:02.262
or unrelated people creates privacy and storage risk without adding value.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:06.387
Plan camera direction, flight path, and retention to minimize unnecessary capture.

00:01:06.387 --> 00:01:10.316
Assess data quality during the mission when safe, then verify after landing.

00:01:10.316 --> 00:01:13.211
Protect media during offload, label it to the flight record,

00:01:13.211 --> 00:01:15.236
and preserve originals when required.

00:01:15.236 --> 00:01:19.830
Data is part of the operation and deserves the same planning and accountability as the

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:19.840
aircraft.
